From 0c84e3fe7a822b6a01360e201fb5c237b3ef3f78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: triippywhale <183076650+triippywhale@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:09:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Shaders: unused descriptors' sizes, paired f16 interpolation
 halves, 16-bit wave sums with lanes gone

Three translator gaps that dropped world shaders (46 programs of the
retail pack; 0 that translated before stop now, by a whole-pack
`translate --validate --list` against the previous commit):

- A descriptor nothing uses as one, whose dwords the code reads all the
  same ("a descriptor read only as data", 35, and one "a descriptor's
  address or format read as data"): an 8-dword image picked from the heap
  by an index in a constant buffer, its width/height/base level turned
  into a texel size (PS_PuddleDetect, 34 pixel programs), or a 4-dword
  buffer tested for being empty by its record count
  (ShallowWaterSim:CS_MinTimestepReduce). New `unused_descriptor_kind`
  gives such loads a kind (image: a 2D texture, documented as a shortcut;
  buffer: a raw view) and `descriptor_data` rebuilds their size dwords from
  the host view as it does for used descriptors; the buffer's address
  dwords come from the host as before. Lane-copied descriptors and
  samplers keep their own handling (checked first).
- The first half of an f16 interpolation pair whose register an f16 second
  half then writes the high half of ("the first half of an
  interpolation", 8, PS_DeferredTextured and mirror-reflection variants):
  the second half keeps the low half of the register, which the first
  half wrote and nothing reads. The first half of a pair now writes 0.
- A 16-bit float wave sum where some lanes have left the program ("a wave
  sum of 16-bit floats where not every lane runs", 2,
  compute_graph_ops:CS_TransposeVecMatMul*): on a host wave of 64 lanes,
  `half_sum_present` follows the console's balanced tree, each lane
  reading its partner run's partial sum from the first lane of that run
  that is here (every lane of an aligned run holds the run's sum on the
  console, the ones outside EXEC included), +0 where none is. Two host
  waves of 32 still refuse it.

Tests: a GPU test of the 16-bit sum with 64, 63, 40, 33, 32, 17, 5 and 1
lanes staying, bit for bit against the console's tree (RX 7900 XT).
cargo test --workspace and clippy -D warnings pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
